      "body": "We've had a couple of PRs for this (#14049 and #14649) which attempt to fix this by filtering the native traceback itself when displaying exception groups.\n\nI think such a fix is too narrow. We should do one of these things instead:\n\n1. Reopen and fix #13023, that is, let `--tb=native` respect `__tracebackhide__` also for regular exceptions. Then, the ExceptionGroup formatting can get the same filtering \"for free\". @The-Compiler had previously closed #13023 with the argument that `--tb=native` is meant for getting full \"raw\" details and so shouldn't filter. I somewhat agree with this, but that said, in the pytest model the tb style (controlled by `--tb`) and whether to filter (controlled by `--fulltrace`) are orthogonal concerns. In this respect it *does* make sense to support filtering in `--tb=native`, and users which want the full traceback would additionally need to pass `--fulltrace`. @The-Compiler WDYT?\n\n2. Add proper tb-style support for ExceptionGroups instead of falling back to native (issue #9159). I have started on this but haven't had time to finish (the hard part if coming up with a nice way to format the exception group tree; the `TerminalRepr` mechanism is not quite up to the task and needs some refinement).\n\nMy opinion is we should do both. Option 1 is relatively straightforward to implement I think (maybe @EternalRights can update #14649, if we decide to reopen #13023).",
