      "body": "> We've had a couple of PRs for this ([#14049](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/pull/14049) and [#14649](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/pull/14649)) which attempt to fix this by filtering the native traceback itself when displaying exception groups.\n> \n> I think such a fix is too narrow. We should do one of these things instead:\n> \n> 1. Reopen and fix [--tb=native should exclude non-user frames #13023](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/13023), that is, let `--tb=native` respect `__tracebackhide__` also for regular exceptions. Then, the ExceptionGroup formatting can get the same filtering \"for free\". [@The-Compiler](https://github.com/The-Compiler) had previously closed [--tb=native should exclude non-user frames #13023](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/13023) with the argument that `--tb=native` is meant for getting full \"raw\" details and so shouldn't filter. I somewhat agree with this, but that said, in the pytest model the tb style (controlled by `--tb`) and whether to filter (controlled by `--fulltrace`) are orthogonal concerns. In this respect it _does_ make sense to support filtering in `--tb=native`, and users which want the full traceback would additionally need to pass `--fulltrace`. [@The-Compiler](https://github.com/The-Compiler) WDYT?\n> 2. Add proper tb-style support for ExceptionGroups instead of falling back to native (issue [Pytest does not show inner exceptions in PEP-654 `ExceptionGroup`s #9159](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/9159)). I have started on this but haven't had time to finish (the hard part if coming up with a nice way to format the exception group tree; the `TerminalRepr` mechanism is not quite up to the task and needs some refinement).\n> \n> My opinion is we should do both. Option 1 is relatively straightforward to implement I think (maybe [@EternalRights](https://github.com/EternalRights) can update [#14649](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/pull/14649), if we decide to reopen [#13023](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/13023)).\n\nMakes sense. I'd be happy to rework #14649 toward option 1 (filtering __tracebackhide__ in --tb=native for all exceptions). I'll wait for a decision on reopening #13023 before pushing changes.\n\nOption 2 is beyond what I can take on right now, but happy to help test if someone picks it up.",
